{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-pro-1-7","title":"Proverbs 1:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Book Introduction - Proverbs Read first chapter of Proverbs This collection of sententious sayings is divine wisdom applied to the earthly conditions of the people of God. That the Proverbs were Solomon's (Proverbs 1:1) implies no more than that he gathered into orderly arrangement sayings already current amongst the people, the wisdom of the Spirit, perhaps through many centuries (Ecclesiastes 12:9). Chapters 25-29 were current in Hezekiah's time (Ecclesiastes 25:1). Chapters 30 and 31 are by Agur and Lemuel. The book is in six parts: To sons, 1-7. The praise of wisdom, 8-9. The folly of sin, 10-19. Warnings and instructions, 20-29. The words of Agur, 30. The words of King Lemuel, 31. fear Also; Proverbs 1:29, (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")</p>"},{"id":"scofield-pro-1-12","title":"Proverbs 1:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>grave Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-pro-1-29","title":"Proverbs 1:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>fear Also; Proverbs 1:7. (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-pro-2-5","title":"Proverbs 2:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>fear Also; Proverbs 3:7, (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-pro-2-21","title":"Proverbs 2:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>perfect (See Scofield \"1 Kings 8:61\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-pro-3-5","title":"Proverbs 3: